{"uid":"7de7676fd47aed92","name":"test_skill_placed_in_operator_home_survives_a_real_subset_from_task_002s_attributed_list","fullName":"tests.test_skills_discoverability_survives_suite#test_skill_placed_in_operator_home_survives_a_real_subset_from_task_002s_attributed_list","historyId":"e539246170c9337feffa116e0f0c8aff","time":{"start":1791969405772,"stop":1791969410944,"duration":5172},"description":"Task 004 (#83): task 002's wipewatch attribution named ten fast-tier\n    node ids that call `amain()` *in-process* (no child spawn) against\n    whatever `HOME` the pytest PROCESS itself has. Task 003 closed that\n    door with an autouse fixture,\n    `tests/conftest.py::_isolate_ambient_home_in_process`, that isolates\n    every test's own `HOME` to a throwaway directory by default. This test\n    proves that fix holds for a real pytest subprocess run drawn straight\n    from task 002's own attributed list, not just a single isolated call:\n    place a skill under an operator-like `$HOME`, run a subset --\n    `tests/test_engine_budget_seed.py` and\n    `tests/test_status_max_approaches.py`, both named in task 002's list and\n    both calling `amain()` directly with no `HOME` override of their own --\n    inside a pytest subprocess whose own environment names that same\n    `$HOME` (via `_run_pytest_subset`), then re-checks the skill is still\n    discoverable by the agent's own rule afterward.\n\n    Reverting task 003's isolation with this exact one-line mutation to\n    `tests/conftest.py::_isolate_ambient_home_in_process` --\n\n        -    monkeypatch.setenv(\"HOME\", str(isolated))\n        +    return\n\n    -- makes this node fail: with the fixture reduced to a no-op, the\n    subprocess's own tests inherit the outer subprocess's `HOME` (the\n    operator-like home this test set up), `amain()` reads it via\n    `ambient_home()`, and `place_skills()`'s clear-then-fill wipes the\n    planted skill directory. See\n    `artifacts/reports/task-009-before-after-mutation-evidence.md`'s\n    section D for the recorded failing node id and both pass/fail counts.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 004 (#83): task 002's wipewatch attribution named ten fast-tier<br />\nnode ids that call <code>amain()</code> <em>in-process</em> (no child spawn) against<br />\nwhatever <code>HOME</code> the pytest PROCESS itself has. Task 003 closed that<br />\ndoor with an autouse fixture,<br />\n<code>tests/conftest.py::_isolate_ambient_home_in_process</code>, that isolates<br />\nevery test's own <code>HOME</code> to a throwaway directory by default. This test<br />\nproves that fix holds for a real pytest subprocess run drawn straight<br />\nfrom task 002's own attributed list, not just a single isolated call:<br />\nplace a skill under an operator-like <code>$HOME</code>, run a subset --<br />\n<code>tests/test_engine_budget_seed.py</code> and<br />\n<code>tests/test_status_max_approaches.py</code>, both named in task 002's list and<br />\nboth calling <code>amain()</code> directly with no <code>HOME</code> override of their own --<br />\ninside a pytest subprocess whose own environment names that same<br />\n<code>$HOME</code> (via <code>_run_pytest_subset</code>), then re-checks the skill is still<br />\ndiscoverable by the agent's own rule afterward.</p>\n<pre><code>Reverting task 003's isolation with this exact one-line mutation to\n`tests/conftest.py::_isolate_ambient_home_in_process` --\n\n    -    monkeypatch.setenv(&quot;HOME&quot;, str(isolated))\n    +    return\n\n-- makes this node fail: with the fixture reduced to a no-op, the\nsubprocess's own tests inherit the outer subprocess's `HOME` (the\noperator-like home this test set up), `amain()` reads it via\n`ambient_home()`, and `place_skills()`'s clear-then-fill wipes the\nplanted skill directory. See\n`artifacts/reports/task-009-before-after-mutation-evidence.md`'s\nsection D for the recorded failing node id and both pass/fail counts.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false